Pseudo code
1. Compute inflow using Biot-Savart law (BEM for the first iteration)
2. Compute radial lift distribution
3. Find circulation strengths from lift distribution. 80% of the peak circulation is tip vortex strength
4. Assume prescribed wake trajectory (Landgrebe’s, or any other)
Iterate until
everything converges


Free Wake Model
oNo empirical wake model.
oVortex segments allowed to get influenced by velocities induced by other segments and move freely in space
oWake shape (position of vortex segments) updated at each time segment
Betoney, Patrick et al. “Development of a
free-vortex wake model in state-space form.” (2009).